  "name": "MPV (MEAN PLATELET VOLUME)",
  "code": "1570",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"59\" data-end=\"242\"><strong data-start=\"59\" data-end=\"89\">MPV (Mean Platelet Volume)</strong> measures the <strong data-start=\"103\" data-end=\"132\">average size of platelets</strong> in the blood. It helps evaluate <strong data-start=\"165\" data-end=\"201\">platelet production and activity</strong> and is reported in <strong data-start=\"221\" data-end=\"241\">femtoliters (fL)</strong>.</p>\n<p data-start=\"59\" data-end=\"242\">MPV is often interpreted <strong data-start=\"1294\" data-end=\"1322\">alongside platelet count</strong>:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Platelet Count</th>\n<th>MPV</th>\n<th>Possible Interpretation</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Low</td>\n<td>High</td>\n<td>Peripheral destruction (e.g., ITP) &ndash; bone marrow is responding by releasing larger platelets</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Low</td>\n<td>Low</td>\n<td>Bone marrow failure or suppression</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>High</td>\n<td>High</td>\n<td>Myeloproliferative disorders or reactive thrombocytosis</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Normal</td>\n<td>Abnormal MPV</td>\n<td>Suggests early or compensated platelet turnover abnormalities</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p data-start=\"59\" data-end=\"242\">&nbsp;</p>",
